    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Tikkun Patch Commit.</strong> When you resolve a bug in reality, you know how to push the fix upstream.</p><ul><li>When your party resolves a <strong>Spark, Tikkun, or hex-tilt scene</strong> in a way that clearly <strong>repairs</strong> something (socially, spiritually, or structurally), you can declare a <em>patch commit</em>.</li><li>Once per such scene, the GM may apply a small <strong>hex-level improvement</strong> to the affected location: a point of <strong>Darkness reduction</strong>, a nudge toward better <strong>hex tilt</strong>, or a minor positive modifier, as appropriate to your campaign rules.</li></ul><p>This feature gives you a repeatable, mechanical way to justify the map getting slightly better wherever you do good Tikkun work.</p>",
